                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Example Office",
                "headline": "Flood Advisory issued October 3 at 6:02PM EDT until October 3 at 9:00PM EDT by NWS Example Office",
                "description": "* WHAT...Urban and small stream flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of the example region, including the following counties, Example and Sample.\n\n* WHEN...Until 900 PM EDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas. Water over roadways. Overflowing poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 602 PM EDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to thunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly in the advisory area. Between 1 and 3 inches of rain have fallen.\n- Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are expected over the area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nExample Town, Sample Village, Northfield, Southfield and Lakeside.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood deaths occur in vehicles.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "FLSXXX"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WGUS00 KXXX 032209"
                    ],
                    "NWSheadline": [
